; link/pop_charprobe.link — THE CHARACTER PROBE's memory map (P5.28; re-laid P5.29).
;
; tile_probe.s assembled with -DCHAR_PROBE, plus char_probe.s (the draw list; its streams, the
; registry and the frame table in section chdata), xf_blit.s (the transform), blit_core.o (its
; identity case) and xf_tables.
;
;   $0E00-....    the program (section `prog`), EXEC address = tile_entry. $0E00 is the LOADM
;                 floor build.bat's map_overlap_check enforces (DECB's buffers end below it).
;   $3000-$41FF   the packed tile page, staged one whole track (tile_probe.s LZ_STAGE) --
;                 written by the program's own disk read, so nothing LOADM'd may live here
;   $4200-$5EFF   xf_blit's TABLES, 7,424 B: M $4200 (PAGE-ALIGNED -- the patched operand's
;                 low byte is the index), T1 $4300, T2 $4400, the nine shift pairs $4500-$56FF,
;                 and P5.29's four SWAP-ONLY pairs $5700-$5EFF (k = 0..3; the colour phase
;                 without the mirror). build.bat passes -DXF_M/-DXF_T1/-DXF_T2/-DXF_TABS.
;   $5F00-$5F11   xf_blit's direct page (-DXF_DPPAGE=0x5F), eighteen bytes (fourteen before P5.34), nothing else
;   $6A00-$6A06   the disk driver's parameter block (-DDR_VARBASE)
;   $6B00-....    section chdata: the baked streams, char_cels.s, frame_table.s
;   $7800-$78FF   trace ring buffer
;   $7900-....    KERNEL (section `code` = hal_build.o)
;   $7F00         stack top
;   $8000-$BBFF   the back buffer; $C000-$DFFF the tile page through $FFA6
;
; ★ WHY NOT $2000 LIKE THE TILE PROBE. Jay, 2026-10-04: "since we are using a loader to start
; the program, after that loadm areas arent important since we only use loadm to boot." The
; LOADM ceiling at $2488..$2535 (link/pop_engine.link) is a constraint on BOOTING; this
; program's code is past it at $2000, so it sits at the floor instead, and its data above the
; driver block. A LOADM of 6,912 B at $4000 was measured to load (idioms §23).

section prog load 0E00
section xftab load 4200
section chdata load 6B00
section code load 7900

entry tile_entry
